@nanjiangwill, refreshed this against the current v0.4 mainline. The cache is wired through the relocated `slime.data.data_source` API, and missing rollout configuration disables it. The transient payload now lives outside the dataclass fields, preserving the new fan-out path that reconstructs Samples from `dataclasses.fields()` while retaining immutable sharing across deep-copied siblings.

Local validation: 111 CPU tests passed, including stock data sources, repeated epochs/siblings, serialization/reconstruction, eval, buffer/checkpoint behavior, fully async rollout, and plugin contracts. The full refreshed [PR Test run](https://github.com/THUDM/slime/actions/runs/37924858339) is green with 89 successful jobs and no failures. Filtering, Sample, buffer, and real distributed Ray/Straw fan-out all passed, as did pre-commit.

The PR is mergeable and ready for another look. The workload benchmark and bounded text-only cache scope are documented in the description.
